## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design scalable multi-tenant data isolation using AWS IAM, Lake Formation, and S3 policies across multiple regions. It explores understanding of cross-region replication, governance controls, and auditability for SaaS applications.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped IAM roles with STS AssumeRole session tags
- Lake Formation permissions and data lake zone isolation
- S3 replication, encryption (SSE-KMS), and access boundaries
- Least-privilege access enforcement through bucket policies
- Auditing with CloudTrail, AWS Config, and Access Analyzer

## Code Example
```javascript
// Trust policy snippet for tenant role
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::${tenant_account_id}:role/TenantUser"},
    "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
    "Condition": {
      "StringEquals": {"aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${tenant_id}"},
      "StringLike": {"aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${tenant_id}"}
    }
  }]
}

// S3 bucket policy for tenant isolation
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Deny",
    "Principal": "*",
    "Action": "s3:*",
    "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::datalake-bucket/*",
    "Condition": {
      "StringNotEquals": {"s3:prefix": ["${tenant_id}/*"]},
      "Bool": {"aws:SecureTransport": "true"}
    }
  }]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses design for fair throughput, scalability, and auditable enforcement in a shared data lake.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant quotas; token bucket; API Gateway usage plans; DynamoDB; Lambda; S3 prefixes; CloudWatch; Kinesis Firehose; testing at scale.

## Code Example
```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, burst) {
    this.rate = rate; // tokens per second
    this.burst = burst;
    this.tokens = burst;
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  allow(n=1){
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.burst, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    this.last = now;
    if (this.tokens >= n) { this.tokens -= n; return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test multi-tenant fairness under bursty conditions and validate SLA guarantees?
- What changes if large tenants typically spike during business hours?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests comprehensive data architecture skills including cross-account streaming, centralized analytics, security controls, disaster recovery, and governance at enterprise scale.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-account IAM role design with least privilege principles
- Kinesis Data Streams vs MSK trade-offs for multi-tenant workloads
- Lake Formation cell-based security and column-level access controls
- Server-side encryption with KMS using per-tenant customer-managed keys
- Multi-region disaster recovery and automated schema evolution strategies

